Hi Hackers!
I have been playing Hack/Nethack for about 6 years now and learnt
many tricks during that time, but when I read this newsgroup, I think
I was playing another game...   ;-)

During the Easter days, I had time enough to hack around with NH3.1.1,
and now I have some questions (that also may apply to earlier versions).


Warning:
The questions _may_ include some spoilers, the answers (hopefully) _will_.


1. My first try was a random character: a tourist. In the Mines, he found
   a "drum of earthquake". After trying out the drum, there were many,
   many pits around. He had no chance for a second try, because some bad
   guy killed him before.
   I wonder what the drum is really good for.
   Will the dungeon collapse, when the drum is hit too much?

2. In this newsgroup, there are many postings about the magic weapons.
   Is there any _legal_ way to find out in the game, that I should wish
   for a "blessed rustproof +20 Dragonblaster" or so?   :-)
   With 'legal', I mean not to look into the binaries or in this newsgroup.
   (One legal method I know already: My Barbarian, Conan of course, found
   a war hammer named Ogresmasher in a shop. But it's not of much use to
   him. He sometimes gets blasted when wielding it.)

3. Is this a bug? :
   Conan the Barbarian has successfully cleared Fort Ludios. Since
   Croesus is dead now, why is there still someone searching the
   empty gold chambers ("You hear someone searching") resp. counting
   the money in the full ones.
   (OK it may be helpful to detect new gold chambers)

4. What can be done against Liches (besides genocide)? They are very nasty.
   Or, more general, is there anything against being cursed?

5. Tourist Harry met Jabberwocky in the Dwarfish Mines, Level 10.
   No chance, of course. But I think, Jabberwocky is tough to kill
   for other people, too. Any tricks?

6. Under some circumstances (I know some of them), a character aggravates
   monsters. If this is an intrinsic, can I get rid of it? (and how?)

7. Conan has also intrinsic teleporting (He ate a tin of ... meat)
   This may be fine when you have a ring of teleport control. 
   Can he get rid of this feature?

8. What is polypiling? How is it done?

9. How can I make an item rustproof? Can I re-new an already rusty item?




   -suddenly, the posting collapses -


